      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "hard_break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Editor-in-chief Professor Stephane Pradines explains how the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Journal of Material Cultures in the Muslim World",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                },
                {
                  "type": "link",
                  "attrs": {
                    "href": "https://www.aku.edu/ismc/publications/Pages/mcmw.aspx",
                    "target": "_blank",
                    "linktype": "url",
                    "uuid": null,
                    "anchor": null,
                    "custom": {}
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " has become the go-to publication for field archaeologists, art historians, anthropologists, curators, scholars and students of material culture in Muslim contexts."
            },
            {
              "type": "hard_break"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Stephane Pradines",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "link",
                  "attrs": {
                    "href": "http://www.aku.edu/ismc/people/Pages/stephane-pradines.aspx",
                    "target": "_blank",
                    "linktype": "url",
                    "uuid": null,
                    "anchor": null,
                    "custom": {}
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " is an archaeologist and Professor of Islamic Art and Architecture at AKU-ISMC in London. Professor Pradines was the Director of the excavations of the Walls of Cairo (Egypt) and many other excavations in the Indian Ocean and East Africa. He is a specialist of Islamic archaeology in Sub-Saharan Africa, Indian Ocean medieval trade and Muslim material culture of war."
            },
            {
              "type": "hard_break"
            },
            {
              "type": "hard_break"
            }
          ]
        },
